[{"id":"VRCE-6-94-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":1,"english":"And as it speedily descended, the monarch of men beheld that Raksasa-king's resounding car, having huge standards, yoked with black chargers, and endowed with fierce splendour; as if flaming in the firmament; having the resplendance of the Sun himself; with thronging lightning pennons; displaying the glow of Indra's weapon* showering arms; and resembling rain-charged clouds. *The rain-blow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ffae1d8b045b680eceba103e9c078b5833c9302adf4a4db8a556a4e0a423388","compact":"9cffdac7a74851785f2408b5254fd3d66a9189d55ae68e0e957f29e257a9cd48","nasal":"3ff8060e0c96915bc6f9fea3492a8ef5d33843d347be062ad2b0046fbf68d747"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":2,"english":"And as it speedily descended, the monarch of men beheld that Raksasa-king's resounding car, having huge standards, yoked with black chargers, and endowed with fierce splendour; as if flaming in the firmament; having the resplendance of the Sun himself; with thronging lightning pennons; displaying the glow of Indra's weapon* showering arms; and resembling rain-charged clouds. *The rain-blow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0ebba89d9e1e13e810b925a25db8d854b830ef4fab65de495a3e713059fddaee","compact":"c6c3f65bc9f0694697927d72a6d015afb76c97f13a72cd7e63a7f07994059703","nasal":"22545b8a7e6fc5e7b5592ffe1e29f5bb023a1b531285cf77e83262317c909973"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":3,"english":"Seeing the enemy's car resembling a mass of clouds having a chatter resembling the sounds sent by a cleaving mountain riven by the thunder, Rāma, vehemently drawing his bow curved like the infant moon, addressed Mătalicharioteer to the thousand-eyed (deity) saying. *Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fbe14403079d509d95cc30d32f3af7ea3ae9a129a81feaf8a86ce9b1dcea2b22","compact":"7155f6b47d0f257c8336bc06d3cb42630855621cf2c4d47335e8ec75e8c378b5","nasal":"2049e5bb4b3ae83af1a8f54235bb26b1df6e456113e1af20b19ef93b2e8ea671"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":4,"english":"O Mătalī, behold the enraged chariot of my foe as it course on. From the furious speed with which he is again wheeling at my right, it appear that he has set his heart of slaying me in encouter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"772f7a65d720ba98a35355a2a5f8726e3eb1550729f8105a62dc98fe249cd374","compact":"5ad0442a0f08c7c4aac2fb976b0915f1e359b273971087d979fcc6066d1e6bfd","nasal":"4ea3593bcc011fbf5b8d4d3399cd0f753b1dd3f722b4930440a84e4141a7d8a4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":5,"english":"Do you therefore heedfully drive the car right against the vehicle of my foe. I wish to destroy this one even as the wind scatter clouds that have appeared.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4e8c190d3122c3a8939a880096bc192d3c459e01b48aed4dc055ed92dc6b196","compact":"dd0accf8b2d6d0118f77c8fb889431c90744e2380c4d722f0595850f4dc3c1c2","nasal":"dd0accf8b2d6d0118f77c8fb889431c90744e2380c4d722f0595850f4dc3c1c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":6,"english":"Do you with all your wits about you, without trepidation, and holding your heart as will as your eye in calmness, swiftly drive the chariot ruled by the reins.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"31d360899df1146c514055a015240dd5eca24d796a590f6b3e40a72d5dc6ddfd","compact":"b6fc5ad7877bd6b831eb430d54b3b03f7692a771648093ae67f266849890038c","nasal":"a2d2885c2e9f5a4448042e43a7f06aad9718b0671fd3f36496baf74cb630246f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":7,"english":"Worthy of Purandara's car, you ought not to be taught by me. Desirous of encounter and my whole soul bent on fight, I simply remind younot teach you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-106-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6094007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c978ae7905398fe516f3f8082455f0320c8988bb07665fe6a8ae1a28f59b73f0","compact":"ac412e208dcea3e5be5660a907ce9aa1b59c5d33e7289c119e0e08053a4b1dd9","nasal":"ac412e208dcea3e5be5660a907ce9aa1b59c5d33e7289c119e0e08053a4b1dd9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-94-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":94,"verse":8,"english":"Pleased with these words of Rāma, the excellent celestial charioteer-Mātalī-drove the car. Then leaving Ravana's mighty car on the right, he enveloped Rāvana with the dust raised by the wheels.","alignment":{"ty